\DOC ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC

\TYPE {ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
On a goal whose conclusion is an implication whose antecedent equates a nest of
state writes applied to a state {t} with a state {u}, it adds assumptions about
{t}, re-stated for {u}, to the assumption list.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments.
{
   A ?- (write ... t = u) ==> P
   ============================  ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC
   A, A' ?- (write ... t = u) ==> P
}
\noindent Here {A'} consists of new assumptions obtained from assumptions in
{A} by replacing the pre-state {t} with the post-state {u}: typically facts of
the form {read c t = v}, {read c t <=> b}, {~read c t}, or more general
properties mentioning {t}, re-stated for {u}. Only assumptions whose components
are untouched by the writes in the antecedent appear in {A'}, so {A'} is
generally a strict subset of the translatable assumptions. In principle {A'}
may be empty, though in every observed trace at least one assumption is added.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single kind of transformation, on goals whose
conclusion is such a state-equation implication.

\ENDDOC
